 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nOptimizer simplify function breaks with TypeError on set operations\n\n#### Description\n\nThe optimizer's simplify function is throwing a `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +: 'set' and 'set'` when processing certain SQL expressions. This appears to be affecting multiple optimization functions that rely on the simplify module.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import optimizer\n\n# This will raise TypeError\nsql = \"SELECT a FROM table WHERE x = 1 AND y = 2\"\noptimized = optimizer.optimize(sql)\n```\n\nThe error occurs when the simplify function attempts to perform set addition operations, which is not supported in Python. Sets can be combined using union operations but not with the `+` operator.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe optimizer should successfully process SQL expressions without throwing TypeError exceptions related to set operations.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\n```\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +: 'set' and 'set'\n```\n\nThis error is affecting multiple optimizer functions including `optimize`, `normalize`, `simplify`, and predicate pushdown operations.\n</issue>\n",
